                <pb facs="0838" n="724" sameAs="frus:frus1931v01/pg724"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">724.3415/1230a: Circular telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the American Diplomatic
                        Representatives in Colombia, Cuba, Mexico, and Uruguay</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-06-22T19:00:00-04:00">June 22, 1931—7
                    p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>All the Governments having agreed on the text of the notes to be delivered to
                    Bolivia and Paraguay, the diplomatic representatives in Washington of the
                    neutral Governments have agreed with the Department that the notes should be
                    delivered to the Bolivian and Paraguayan Governments on Thursday, June 25.
                    Please so inform the Government to which you are accredited.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
